%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: dc89aefee193f4f74a463defc586dce3, type: 3}
  m_Name: CampaignStory
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::DuckAdventure.Agent.MarshStory
  entries:
  - id: intro
    speaker: Ada's field letter
    oncePerRun: 1
    requiredCapability: 
    prerequisites: []
    pages:
    - "Aiken \u2014 the storm has jammed the five sluices. I took the ducklings to
      Lantern Haven. Duckduckgoose knows their voices. Bring him east, and bring
      three brass coins."
    - A bell does not take a toll. Lend it three coins to lower the causeway. Its
      return tray waits on the far bank. Follow the raised stones; avoid the marsh
      mites on the rust-colored patrol tracks.
  - id: letter
    speaker: Aiken
    oncePerRun: 0
    requiredCapability: 
    prerequisites: []
    pages:
    - Ada's writing leans uphill, even when the water rises. Three coins, five bells,
      one very determined duck. All right, Duckduckgoose. Let's find your family.
  - id: bell1
    speaker: The landing bell
    oncePerRun: 1
    requiredCapability: 
    prerequisites: []
    pages:
    - Three brass notes roll over the reeds. Beneath the water, wooden steps rise
      and catch on their latches.
    - Duckduckgoose lifts his head. One answering peep comes from far to the east.
      Cross the causeway, then press E at the brass tray to reclaim your coins.
  - id: ledger
    speaker: The reed ledger
    oncePerRun: 0
    requiredCapability: 
    prerequisites: []
    pages:
    - "KEEPER'S RULE: Never keep what a traveler needs for the next crossing. The
      bell borrows the weight; the latch does the work. \u2014 Ada"
    - Below it, someone has drawn a duck with a crown. Aiken suspects Duckduckgoose
      has been supervising.
  - id: flood
    speaker: Ada's flood note
    oncePerRun: 0
    requiredCapability: 
    prerequisites: []
    pages:
    - 'Ada''s flood note: ''Four ducklings are safe in the Haven. The youngest has
      a hurt wing. Duckduckgoose went west when the paths failed. Keep every borrowed
      coin moving; the flock is waiting for a way to bring everyone home.'''
    - The storm channel is narrow. Wait for a mite to pass, then follow the stones.
      The lantern landings restore your health. We will keep a light for you.
  - id: bell2
    speaker: The archive bell
    oncePerRun: 1
    requiredCapability: 
    prerequisites: []
    pages:
    - The archive bell joins the earlier notes. Duckduckgoose answers with a sound
      much larger than he is.
    - 'A small chorus answers. They are still together. Aiken checks the far-side
      tray: the same three coins, warm from the mechanism, ready for the locks ahead.'
  - id: promise
    speaker: The keeper's promise
    oncePerRun: 0
    requiredCapability: 
    prerequisites: []
    pages:
    - "A safe path is a promise made to someone you may never meet. Leave the steps
      raised. Leave the bells ready. Bring each other home. \u2014 Ada "
  - id: bell3
    speaker: The haven bell
    oncePerRun: 1
    requiredCapability: 
    prerequisites: []
    pages:
    - The last bell rings. Across the water, four small shapes gather at the light.
    - Duckduckgoose stops listening and starts hurrying. The final causeway is raised.
      Lantern Haven is just east of the return tray.
  - id: ending
    speaker: Aiken and Ada
    oncePerRun: 1
    requiredCapability: 
    prerequisites: []
    pages:
    - Duckduckgoose disappears into a tumble of wings and delighted peeps. Ada sets
      down her lantern. 'I knew you would hear us.'
    - Aiken leaves the last causeway latched. Three borrowed coins have opened a
      way for everyone. Behind them, the bells keep speaking across the dark water.
  - id: exchange
    speaker: Ada's counterweight plate
    oncePerRun: 1
    requiredCapability: 
    prerequisites: []
    pages:
    - Two coins in the reed cup lower the distant SOUTH arm. One in the spill cup
      lowers the nearer NORTH arm. Either cup can be filled first. The brass links
      show which weight moves which arm.
    - Reclaim the reed pair from the middle tray, then lend that same pair to the
      EXIT cup. Its shutter opens only after the pair has been recovered. Take the
      spill coin and the exit pair with you. Every latch holds; every coin comes
      back.
  - id: archive-pocket
    speaker: A dry page from the ledger
    oncePerRun: 0
    requiredCapability: 
    prerequisites: []
    pages:
    - Four names, four dry blankets, four bowls of grain. Beneath Ada's careful count,
      a damp webbed footprint has become a fifth mark. Aiken smiles. Duckduckgoose
      had not been counting the flock. He had been making sure Ada had a place, too.
  - id: sword
    speaker: Ada's sword note
    oncePerRun: 1
    requiredCapability: 
    prerequisites: []
    pages:
    - "Aiken \u2014 my reedkeeper's sword is yours. A coin in its guard balances
      each swing, then comes straight back. J or left mouse swipes toward the way
      you last moved. Q equips the blade or packs it away."
    - 'Marsh mites bruise the bank roots. Three clean strikes send one back into
      the mud. The bells still need their own weights: reclaim a coin before fighting
      if every coin is lent. Leave every crossing open for the next traveler.'
  - id: perch-intro
    speaker: Aiken
    oncePerRun: 1
    requiredCapability: perch
    prerequisites: []
    pages:
    - 'Duckduckgoose studies the reed perch as if he has seen it before. Aiken: ''Will
      you hold the lever while I inspect the latch?'' E at the perch calls him; E
      at INSPECT inside latches the shutter. Call or recall is always free.'
  - id: reedbank-bell
    speaker: The listening reeds
    oncePerRun: 1
    requiredCapability: 
    prerequisites: []
    pages:
    - A second bell answers the first. Duckduckgoose listens beyond the chorus, waiting
      for one more voice. Aiken checks the return box. The same three coins are waiting.
  - id: lantern-intro
    speaker: Ada's inspection note
    oncePerRun: 1
    requiredCapability: lantern
    prerequisites: []
    pages:
    - 'Ada''s note: ''One coin warms the inspection lamp. Read the scratched figures,
      then take the coin back with E. Light helps us notice; it is not another toll.'''
  - id: sluice-warning
    speaker: Ada's repair note
    oncePerRun: 1
    requiredCapability: 
    prerequisites:
    - bell2
    pages:
    - The old sluice tender is jammed farther along the route. A lowered head means
      a charge; a raised arm means a sweep. Step clear of the warning and work during
      its recovery. The dry lantern is a safe place to prepare.
  - id: mail-route
    speaker: Ada
    oncePerRun: 1
    requiredCapability: routing
    prerequisites: []
    pages:
    - The sorting box borrows two coins. Its LOW return is open; the HIGH return
      lies in the perch room. E at the sorter changes the address without borrowing
      again. Claim the same two coins at your chosen box before the next bell.
